  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Is a Tub-to-Shower Conversion Right for My Home?",
    "text": "Is a Tub-to-Shower Conversion Right for My Home?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "A tub-to-shower conversion is a popular remodel, and for good reason! But how do you know if it's the right move for *your* home and needs? Well, if you rarely use your bathtub and find yourself wishing for a more spacious, accessible shower, it's definitely worth considering. Many homeowners are looking to modernize their bathrooms, improve accessibility, or simply create a more functional space. Think about your lifestyle: do you prefer quick showers over long soaks? Are you planning for future accessibility needs, perhaps with a curbless entry? These are all great reasons to convert. This type of project can also really open up a smaller bathroom, making it feel much larger and more contemporary. On the other hand, if your home only has one bathroom and you have young children, keeping a tub might be more practical for bathing. It's a balance! We can remove your tub cleanly, modify the subfloor for drainage, and install a brand new shower with proper waterproofing. The key is making sure the new layout fits your home's structure and your personal preferences. Give HH Remodeling LLC a call, and we can explore what makes the most sense for your Aurora home.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}